## Purpose

Operator and marketing surfaces in Kitchen Sink use **WAI-ARIA tablists**—especially `render_fs_tab_panel()` in `components/enterprise_marketing.py`, which emits **`.fs-tab-panel`**, **`.nav.nav-tabs.fs-tab-panel__tabs`**, Bootstrap **`data-bs-toggle="tab"`**, and paired **`role="tabpanel"`** panes. Screen readers and keyboard users need the **selected** tab to declare which panel is active: `aria-selected="true"`, `aria-controls` pointing at the panel element id, and a panel that is **not** `hidden`, `aria-hidden="true"`, or styled `display:none` / `visibility:hidden`.

`det-app-tab-panel.check.js` scans every `[role="tablist"]` on the page. It resolves the active tab as the first `[role="tab"]` with `aria-selected="true"` or the Bootstrap **`.active`** class; if none match, it evaluates the first tab. Violations: **`aria-selected-missing`**, **`missing-aria-controls`**, **`panel-hidden-or-missing`**.

**Plan:** Audit handbook script demos, enterprise tab sections, and app workspace mode switchers that use `role="tablist"`. **Do:** Mirror the canonical `render_fs_tab_panel()` contract on hand-authored markup. **Check:** `tabPanelReport.violations` is empty after metrics collection. **Adjust:** Sync `aria-selected` with the visible `.active` tab, wire `aria-controls` to pane ids, and show exactly one visible panel per selection.

## Passing signals

- Selected tab has **`aria-selected="true"`**; inactive tabs use **`aria-selected="false"`** (not omitted while visually active).
- Every selected tab has **`aria-controls`** equal to the **`id`** of its `role="tabpanel"` pane (same ids used in `data-bs-target="#…"`).
- The controlled panel is **visible**: no `hidden` attribute, no `aria-hidden="true"`, and computed `display` / `visibility` are not hiding it.
- Inactive panes use Bootstrap **`tab-pane fade`** without **`show active`**, or equivalent `hidden` / `aria-hidden` while the active pane carries **`show active`**.
- KS tab sections include realistic chrome: **`section.fs-tab-panel`**, **`ul.fs-tab-panel__tabs`**, **`div.tab-content.fs-tab-panel__panes`**, **`div.fs-tab-panel__body`**, and governed hash attrs when emitted from Python (`hash`, `data-ks-hash`, `data-ks-type`, `data-ks-name`).
- `tabPanelReport.violations` is empty on audited URLs.

## Failing signals

- **`aria-selected-missing`** — tab has **`.active`** / `nav-link active` but `aria-selected` is not **`"true"`** (common when only Bootstrap CSS marks selection).
- **`missing-aria-controls`** — selected or first tab has no **`aria-controls`**, or `data-bs-target` exists without a matching **`aria-controls`** id reference.
- **`panel-hidden-or-missing`** — `aria-controls` points at a missing id, or the panel has **`hidden`**, **`aria-hidden="true"`**, or is CSS-hidden while its tab is selected.
- Multiple panels marked **`show active`** while one tab claims selection—users see one tab label but another panel's content (fix panel visibility, not only tab styles).
- Tablist inside **`main`** without **`aria-label`** on `[role="tablist"]` (accessibility hygiene; pair with `DET.APP.CONTROL_A11Y` when roles/states on controls are wrong).
- Evidence shapes: `tablist="#fs-product-tabs" issue=aria-selected-missing`; `issue=missing-aria-controls`; `issue=panel-hidden-or-missing`.

